    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474-a1">

                <pb facs="0565" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg483"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Three enclosures.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Bigelow to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 243.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation,
                            Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 16, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Recalling my despatch No. 202, I have the
                    honor to transmit a reply, received last evening, from his excellency the
                    minister of foreign affairs to the note which I addressed him on the 22d of
                    November last, in reference to certain decrees promulgated recently from the
                    city of Mexico.</p>
                <p>My letter acknowledging the receipt of his excellency’s communication is also
                    enclosed.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, with great respect, your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
